Parity disposition: the web <ComboboxMulti> is a generic <T> WAI-ARIA multi-select combobox whose value is
an ARRAY — selected options render as removable chips inside the field, and the dropdown ALWAYS hides
already-selected options (the user never sees the same row twice). Its hooks are useTranslation /
useAnnouncer / useId — NO React-Query, NO fetch beyond its own async `options` loader. REAL source
branches reproduced: the chip strip (web value.map), in-flight loading row + inline spinner (web `loading`
/ `asyncLoading`), the empty row whose copy is "Maximum reached" at the cap else "No results", the
populated list with active-descendant highlight (rows non-interactive at the cap), the
"{{count}} more — refine search" overflow footer, the chevron toggle, Backspace-removes-last, the
`maxItems` cap with the ({count}/{max}) label suffix, and the result-count + "Removed {label}"
live-region announce. The async loader's reject folds to [] in the web; this surface, like the in-tree
single-select sibling Combobox (0148) and the forms sibling UnitInput (0162), ADDS the P4 leaf contract so
the field never collapses to a blank box: an explicit error retry row (the QueryError peer of the swallowed
loader failure) + the orthogonal stale/offline freshness axis (chip + one-shot stale auto-refresh). No web
Tailwind class is ported; layout uses P1/S9 tokens. Charts/maps: NONE in source → none here.

Native-idiom note: the web field renders chips + the input on one flex-wrap row; the native peer keeps the
chips inside the same bordered field chrome as a wrapping chip strip above the typing row (the in-tree
TagInput 0160 precedent), HIG-friendly on iPhone. The dropdown is an inline expanding listbox; the keyboard
contract is wired via .onKeyPress for hardware keyboards (macOS / iPadOS) + tap for touch.

